s2_notes.text:
a Possibility to be misannotated. It represents percentages of ptotein homologs have a shorter N-terminal than the query protein (standard: the hits should have a subject start as 1 and a query start no less than 1);
b Possibility to be leaderless transcripts. It represents percentages of protein homologs have a exact same N-terminal as the query protein (standard: the hits should have a subject start as 1 and a query start also as 1; should be a gTSS);
c Hit_counts represent the hits after blastP analysis with a limited maximum hit number as 100 and a e-value less than 1e-5;
d It represents percentages of hits with a subject start as 1 among all hits;
e It represents percentages of hits with a query start no less than 1, among hits with a subject start as 1.
